# Antigravity. With a Google-account sign-in, model traffic and account state go to one of the two hosts below,
# chosen by account kind. daily-cloudcode-pa is a production endpoint despite its name.
# - Google's Code Assist page names cloudcode-pa, "an internal API that provides IDE-related features":
#   https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini/docs/codeassist/set-up-gemini
# - The enterprise doc lists cloudcode-pa as "Cloud Code Telemetry & Client Services", which a Business sign-in reaches
#   in every location (the Business mode, below).
# - No page that was read names daily-cloudcode-pa or the split. agy's own log under ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/log/
#   shows the split after a consumer sign-in.
allow https://cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com/        read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # GCP-licensed and Business
allow https://daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com/  read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # consumer: AI Pro/Ultra/One/Free

# Google-account sign-in, consumer and Business alike. The browser on the host opens the printed sign-in URL on
# accounts.google.com. agy itself sent that host nothing in a consumer sign-in, so the host has no line.
allow https://oauth2.googleapis.com/              read method=POST,PUT,PATCH,DELETE  # code exchange, token refresh

# Eligibility check. Signed in, agy reads the account at userinfo, then the profile picture at the URL that the
# `picture` field names. A refusal at either host shows agy's "Eligibility check failed" banner, with the model list
# loaded.
# Google constrains `picture` only to a URL, not to a host or path. Google's examples use this host with paths of
# different shapes, so the rule allows the whole host:
# https://developers.google.com/identity/openid-connect/reference
# https://developers.google.com/identity/siwg/security-bundle
# https://developers.google.com/identity/gsi/web/reference/js-reference
allow https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v2/userinfo read
allow https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/            read

# The modes below have no line, since no measurement covers them, and the proxy's refusal names the host. A workspace
# that uses one adds its hosts to .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/rule as `allow https://HOST/ tunnel` lines.
# - /voice under --audio=mic streams the recording to aicode.googleapis.com over gRPC, which needs HTTP/2 and so a
#   tunnel (TODO.md, "Deferred — an HTTP/2 relay for gRPC hosts"). Refused, /voice shows "Could not start
#   transcription" (agy 1.3.4). agy 1.5.8 also asks the host for its flags at each start, logs "AICode FetchConfig
#   failed, falling back to CCPA ListExperiments" when refused, and completes its turns.
# - GEMINI_API_KEY, the Gemini API with no sign-in, which also needs "modelProvider": "gemini" in agy's settings.json:
#   generativelanguage.googleapis.com (https://antigravity.google/docs/cli/install).
# - Business sign-in with a Gemini Enterprise license in a Google Cloud project: businessaicode.googleapis.com and
#   aiplatform.googleapis.com, and for the `us` or `eu` location also businessaicode.<location>.rep.googleapis.com and
#   aiplatform.<location>.rep.googleapis.com.
#   - https://antigravity.google/docs/enterprise, "Network allowlists and mTLS endpoints": the client reaches the
#     global businessaicode and cloudcode-pa hosts at sign-in in every location, for the licenses and the model
#     catalog, then sends inference to the location's rep host. The allowlist also names Discovery Engine hosts and
#     mTLS variants for the Antigravity App, CLI and IDEs together.
#   - SECURITY.md, "Not defended", has what an aiplatform tunnel opens to the signed-in credential.
#   - Advanced WIF sign-in also exchanges tokens at sts.googleapis.com and iamcredentials.googleapis.com.
# The Business and API-key modes come from agy's changelog entries 1.1.10 and 1.1.13:
# https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md

# play.googleapis.com serves telemetry and experiment polling. The host is absent, as ab.chatgpt.com is absent from
# model-provider/openai.

# Measured with agy 1.5.8 on 2026-11-14, signed in with a consumer account, under deny-unless-allowed
# (doc/plan-tls-inspect-agents.md, "Measurement"):
# - Modes: agy -p with a shell call and a subagent that makes its own shell call; agy --conversation -p with a shell
#   call; the interactive TUI in this repository, with two turns and /compact, a sign-out, a sign-in and a message,
#   then /voice under --audio=mic; a token refresh, forced by moving the token file's expiry into the past; the TUI
#   with a turn under deny-unless-model.
# - The path, refused and error lines are what MeasurementReport accepts (doc/plan-tls-inspect-agents.md, "The
#   measurement suite"). Each <...> stands for one segment.
#   path daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com /v1internal:loadCodeAssist /v1internal:fetchAvailableModels
#   path daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com /v1internal:fetchAdminControls /v1internal:fetchUserInfo
#   path daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com /v1internal:retrieveUserQuotaSummary /v1internal:listExperiments
#   path daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com /v1internal:streamGenerateContent /v1internal:writeTrajectoryAcls
#   path daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com /v1internal:recordTrajectoryAnalytics /v1internal/cascadeNuxes
#   path oauth2.googleapis.com /token
#   path www.googleapis.com /oauth2/v2/userinfo
#   path lh3.googleusercontent.com /a/<picture>
#   path github.com /<owner>/<repo>
#   refused play.googleapis.com CONNECT
#   refused www.gstatic.com CONNECT
#   refused github.com CONNECT
#   refused aicode.googleapis.com CONNECT
#   error daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com tunnel: Connection reset
#   error daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com client closed before sending a request
#   error daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com relay: Broken pipe
# - The client negotiated HTTP/1.1 and trusted the launch CA. The language server sends the model requests as
#   antigravity/cli/1.5.8; the sign-in, userinfo and picture requests are Go-http-client/1.1.
# - Within each sign-in, the model host's requests and the userinfo read carried the same credential index. The token
#   endpoint's codes and tokens travel in bodies, so its lines carry no cred=.
# - streamGenerateContent bodies are chunked, with ?alt=sse in the query; every other body declared a Content-Length.
#   No query held a credential.
# - After each turn, recordTrajectoryAnalytics uploaded 37 to 208 KB to the model host.
# - In this repository, the TUI sent github.com a HEAD of the repository's own path, without a credential, after a
#   turn. Under deny-unless-model, which admits no catalog host, the proxy refused that CONNECT, and the turn
#   completed.
# - The sign-out sent no request. The sign-in exchanged its code at oauth2.googleapis.com/token; without a D-Bus
#   session, agy keeps the token in ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/antigravity-oauth-token.
# - Other Google clients in a session, such as gcloud, exchange their tokens at oauth2.googleapis.com too. Only agy's
#   exchange and refresh are measured.
# - The refusals: play.googleapis.com (telemetry), every few seconds while agy runs; www.gstatic.com (the plugin
#   marketplace), at the TUI's start; aicode.googleapis.com (the flags), at each start. agy works without them.
# - The errors, each at a process's exit: a connection that agy closed or reset without a request; and the response to
#   a recordTrajectoryAnalytics upload that agy abandoned ("context canceled" in agy's log), whose relay to agy failed
#   with Broken pipe.
# - /voice and fetchConfig went through a tunnel to aicode.googleapis.com, which the measurement allowed. No mode or
#   turn failed.
# - Unmeasured: the GCP-licensed accounts on cloudcode-pa, inspected on this client's evidence; the Business sign-in;
#   GEMINI_API_KEY, whose key may travel in the query (doc/plan-tls-inspect-agents.md, "Guarantees", 3).
